## 🔁 SOC L1 Triage Workflow (Executed)

The lab provides a structured triage flow which mirrors common SOC operations: [file:47][page:1]

### Initial actions (ownership & readiness)
- Select the first priority alert from the queue. [file:47]
- **Assign the alert to yourself** (avoid duplicate effort across analysts). [file:47][page:1]
- Move alert status to **In Progress**. [file:47][page:1]
- Read alert name + description, and capture key indicators (host/user/IP). [file:47][page:1]

### Investigation (decision-making stage)
If a workbook/playbook exists, follow it; if not, investigate directly in SIEM/EDR logs. [page:1][file:47]  
Key investigation guidance emphasized in the room: [page:1]
- Identify **who/what is under threat** (affected user/host/service/cloud).  
- Understand **the action** (login anomaly, malware behavior, phishing indicator, etc.).  
- Review **surrounding events** before/after alert time.  
- Use threat intel or other resources to verify assumptions when needed.

### Final actions (resolution)
- Decide verdict: **True Positive** (real threat) or **False Positive** (benign/noise). [page:1]
- Write a concise, evidence-based analyst comment (reasoning + key pivots). [page:1]
- Close the alert (**Closed**) or escalate to L2 if required. [file:47][page:1]

